Short Brief
This method checks if a number is a palindrome by reversing it and comparing it with the original number. If both match, it returns true; otherwise, it returns false. Negative numbers are immediately rejected since they cannot be palindromes.

Complexities


Time Complexity: O(d)
(where d is the number of digits in the number)


Space Complexity: O(1)
(uses only a few variables, no extra space)

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(int x) {
        int reverse=0;
        int xcopy=x;

        if(x<0){
            return false;
        }

        while(x>0){
            reverse=(reverse*10)+(x%10);
            x/=10;

        }
        return reverse==xcopy;
    }
}
